From c62ec8a06f86fa01a7ec51b0dd0b06143f27c1a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 06:38:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: DKG keygen, closed committee set, CSPRNG in
 replay_harness, drop stale scripts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1) orchestrate.js: replace single trusted-dealer keygen with distributed key
   generation (Feldman VSS / DKG) — sk = Σ party polynomials, no single party
   knows it; committeePK and shares are now DKG-derived (backs the coordinator-free
   key-generation claim that dkg.js demonstrates).
2) DAOVote.sol (both copies): pass the committee {id => pk_j} set in the constructor
   (closed set) and remove the unauthenticated open registerCommitteeMember
   (prevents front-running / injecting unrelated pk). measure_e2e.js updated to pass
   _ids/_pks at deploy.
3) replay_harness.js: Math.random() -> crypto.randomBytes CSPRNG (consistency with
   the rest of the artifact).
4) Remove stale/broken scripts that target an abandoned architecture (single
   Groth16Verifier, on-chain Chaum-Pedersen, bn254, old constructor/method
   signatures): measure_all_gas.js, measure_real_gas.js, measure_real_partial_decrypt.js,
   parallel_harness.js.

orchestrate.js DKG self-check passes (winner=1, cm binding consistent).
